{
  "case_id": "2022-21-442",
  "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Parker Rider-Longmaid",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A claim modeled after Skinner accrues at the end of the state court litigation seeking DNA testing. There are two sets of reasons why, one doctrinal, the other practical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, could you spend a minute on precisely what your liberty interests in -- you've been deprived, that your -- that your client have been -- has been deprived of and who deprived him of it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Parker Rider-Longmaid",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, of -- of course. As the Court recognized in Osborne, the -- the liberty interest is proving one's innocence with newly discovered evidence. And so, as the Court said in Osborne, as a matter of procedural due process, the procedures need to be fair to vindicate that interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm assuming you know our own finality rule, Court Rule 13.3 --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Could you have filed your 1983 complaint right after the -- the Court of Criminal Appeals' decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Parker Rider-Longmaid",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the injury, Your Honor, is the deprivation without due process of the liberty interest and proving your evidence -- proving your innocence with newly discovered evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Okay. Thank you.\nThat's very helpful.\nA quick question on the Article III\npoint. Why didn't you seek an injunction? Why\ndid you do declaratory judgment instead?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rider-Longmaid",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RIDER-LONGMAID: I -- I think a\nfew points, Your Honor. The first is that it's,\nof course, not necessary. We pointed in the\nbriefing to Franklin versus Massachusetts --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rider-Longmaid",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RIDER-LONGMAID: So I -- what --\nwhat I'd like to do is -- is perhaps move to the\npractical considerations and the -- and the\nproblems with Fifth Circuit's rule on Goertz's\nrule.\nAs -- as I stated in the opening, if\nthe -- on the Fifth Circuit's rule, the injury,\nthe only injury that the Fifth Circuit seemed to\ncare about occurs when the trial court first\ndenies testing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, suppose the\ndifference is between a rule that says the\nstatute of limitations runs when the Court of\nCriminal Appeals renders its decision and a rule\nthat says it doesn't begin to run until\nrehearing is denied. Then you're talking about\na -- a brief period of time, I would imagine, in\nmost cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: Thank you, Mr. Chief\nJustice, and may it please the Court:\nReed's claim is both jurisdictionally\nbarred and untimely. On jurisdiction, the\ndefendant Reed named, the claim he brought, and\nthe relief he seeks don't line up.\nReed sued Goertz for a declaration\nregarding Chapter 64, but Chapter 64 governs\nonly access to testing through Texas courts. It\ndoes not control Goertz's common law authority\nto agree to testing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: Respectfully, I disagree, Your Honor, for two reasons, the more important one being that the petition that Mr. Reed sought under Section 1257 to this Court was a proper vehicle for alleging a due process problem in the Court of Criminal Appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: So you're saying there's no 1983 claim that could be brought to enforce an Article 64 right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: Two points, Your Honor. First, as this Court puts in --in Steel Co., essentially, implied exercises or blessings of jurisdiction that are not actually made holdings of the Court don't bind the Court going forward."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now the Court did make a jurisdictional determination regarding Rooker-Feldman that I think actually is important in this case also because the Court determined in its opinion specifically relying on a concession that's not been made by Mr. Reed, specifically that his claim was not challenging anything that either the prosecutor did or that the Court of Criminal Appeals did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: It seems to me the question here involves tension between two -- two principles. One is the principle that a state does not deny procedural due process until the state-provided procedures have ended, and the other is that a person bringing a 1983 claim, including presumably a 1983 due process claim, does not have to exhaust state remedies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Yes. So even if he has a full and complete cause of action after the trial court rules, which is what I understood you to say in response to Justice Barrett, do you dispute that in determining when Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I -- I guess what I'm worried about is the suggestion that the accrual date necessarily has to start from a moment in which you can identify an injury such as you have in this case when, in cases like McDonough and Manuel, the Court seems to suggest that the accrual date is set in light of other considerations, including the fact that in this case you would have parallel litigation if you set the accrual date early."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Parker Rider-Longmaid",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Alito and Justice Barrett asked about I think the exhaustion question and whether exhaustion would be required."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Reed has a stay of execution from the Texas courts on his ninth subsequent habeas petition before the courts where he raised evidence that Fennell admitted to killing Stites because he discovered she was sleeping with a black man, that Fennell threatened to kill Stites if he caught her cheating, that Fennell made inculpatory statements at Stites' funeral and that Fennell and Stites' relationship was fraught."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-442",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb711db546a54e09824c8d8940f362ec22731ff09585fe7709af2d63cdab9a92",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb711db546a5-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 1:16 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
